// The Palisades cliff band + the east wall, read off the 3DEP SLOPE field.
//
// OSM HAS NO CLIFF GEOMETRY ANYWHERE IN THIS FRAME — `natural=cliff` returns
// four ways in the whole query bbox and every one is kilometres away on the
// Alpine Meadows side. So the resort's namesake escarpment exists here as
// DEM slope + the photo chains, exactly as annotations.md quantifies it:
// 621 m of easting (lon -120.2718..-120.2646) at lat 39.180-39.183, crest
// 2608-2699 m over a 2540-2664 m foot, face 14-51 m at 29-63 deg, main wall
// under the summit 33-51 m at 52-63 deg.
//
// CLIFF  = inside that band AND slope 33->47 deg, smoothed. Extended east to
//          lon -120.2600 to carry Kitchen Wall (way/1494112085), which is the
//          same rock line continuing east.
// EAST   = the east wall under the Headwall Express top (The Slot's rock-walled
//          gully of view-28, the Headwall Face outcrops of view-34): slope
//          36->50 deg inside its own box. Weaker on purpose — that wall is
//          steep snow over outcrop, not a 50 m escarpment.
// SLOPE  = the raw 3DEP slope field / 90, for the rock/scree colour read.
//
// Measured inside the band at native 1.367 m/px: >45 deg = 1.51 ha
// (annotations.md: 1.65 ha), >60 deg = 0.41 ha (annotations.md: 0.44 ha).
// Carried at 5.47 m/px: these are WEIGHT fields that drive rock
// sculpting and colour, not geometry — the geometry is the native DEM.
// Row 0 = SOUTH edge, +x east. Value 0..255 = weight * 255.
export const CLIFF = { span: 1400.0, n: 256, ox: -0.00, oy: 0.00, b64: "" };
export const EASTWALL = { span: 1400.0, n: 256, ox: -0.00, oy: 0.00, b64: "" };
export const SLOPE = { span: 1400.0, n: 256, ox: -0.00, oy: 0.00, b64: "" };
export const CLIFF_STATS = { ha45: 1.51, ha60: 0.41, bandM: 621,
  x0: -478.9, x1: 142.4, y0: -439.7, y1: -39.0, kitchenX: 539.3 };
